  "notes": "A producer's model, so it is his workflow rather than a rapper's cadence — and the workflow has one governing tension the research states outright: **replayed, slightly-off-grid orchestral parts over a rigid programmed grid**. That is authored as a split. `session.humanize.quantizeStrength` drops to 0.72 — the loosest on this axis — because when a loop will not clear he has it replayed note-for-note and then sped up, which is a human string or keys part; but `timingJitterMs` on the drum lanes is dialled to 0 or 1, because the kit underneath does not move. Neither number means anything without the other. ⛔ The second signature is the 808: the research says the bass line is **played in after the fact rather than programmed with the kit**, so `drums.kick.lockTo808` drops from trap's 1.0 to 0.45 and the sub becomes a written melodic part — `legato`, `slideProb` 0.15 (\"few slides\"), a 19-semitone register so it can actually carry a tune, and `melodicallyIndependent`. Everywhere else in this batch the kick and the 808 are one instrument played twice; here they are two parts. ⚠ `melody.monophonicBias` 0.4 is the octave-doubled top line the research names — the lowest figure in this batch by a distance, so roughly three notes in five arrive doubled. `phraseBars` [4,8] and `structure: long_arc` are the 4- and 8-bar minor loops; `contour` is arch-and-descend rather than riff because strings and brass are the material, not a bell ostinato. The i–VI–VII and i–VII–VI families are named verbatim in the research and carry the top two weights. ⚠ `arrangement.dropByBar` 9 is the 4- or 8-bar melodic intro *before the drums*, and `dropOutBeats.beats` 4 is the drop-out to strings under the last hook. `confidence` is high: a per-record production account plus an album-length oral history is the best sourcing anything in this batch has. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.45 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.45 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
